<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-04-23T22:34:49.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 18754,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "###Balancing AI & Human Skills\n\nAI can help us think, write, and solve problems. But how do we use it without weakening our own skills?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/ee5cc96a8a5c834333ec656df40047e1-panel0.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-61c12f93-e668-4a3b-ab10-8b09009a01a3",
        "layout": "text-top-center",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "Brain Skills",
            "x": 42,
            "y": 76,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-371c1d10-09fe-49b6-8cd1-f79f8f6ee6bf",
            "width": 9
          },
          {
            "text": "The Pilot Analogy",
            "x": 72,
            "y": 62,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-0c70d15f-04dc-42e5-8c8e-6a62cafa5f48",
            "width": 13
          },
          {
            "text": "Smart AI Use",
            "x": 28,
            "y": 50,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-c16be7f1-46e7-4448-997e-d22428db25ea",
            "width": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "#What happens to your brain when AI does the thinking?\nYour brain is like a muscle and if you stop using certain skills, they get weaker over time. Using AI for everything can make you miss the practice that keeps your brain strong.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/dd1e7a1c422b5005f83b8dc18b6cc82c-one_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-371c1d10-09fe-49b6-8cd1-f79f8f6ee6bf",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "Generate to Remember",
            "x": 11,
            "y": 36,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-90b1d169-1598-430a-94ed-8b32367dbe0f",
            "width": 15
          },
          {
            "text": "The Memory Trap",
            "x": 53,
            "y": 60,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-d8f2b85b-3a5e-4133-a024-2381dcceff16",
            "width": 11
          },
          {
            "text": "The Muscle Effect",
            "x": 42,
            "y": 18,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-bed6cab6-30c1-4d4e-8e8f-694f3b73f732",
            "width": 15
          },
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 85,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-61c12f93-e668-4a3b-ab10-8b09009a01a3",
            "width": 15
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When people use tools to remember things for them, they are less likely to remember that information later.\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/b148818445f9a92f03698377f661fb06-oneone_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-90b1d169-1598-430a-94ed-8b32367dbe0f",
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-371c1d10-09fe-49b6-8cd1-f79f8f6ee6bf",
            "width": 17
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Students remember information better when they come up with their own answers instead of just reading them.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/8c718c09a0234f1a3bd67c83e88612b8-onetwo_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-d8f2b85b-3a5e-4133-a024-2381dcceff16",
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-371c1d10-09fe-49b6-8cd1-f79f8f6ee6bf",
            "width": 16
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "When you practice a skill, it builds stronger connections in your brain, making that skill faster and easier over time.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/7f4bf4d78f317b197c197224396c6f8a-onethree_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-bed6cab6-30c1-4d4e-8e8f-694f3b73f732",
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 16,
            "y": 86,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-371c1d10-09fe-49b6-8cd1-f79f8f6ee6bf",
            "width": 16
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "#Which tasks should AI handle — and which should humans keep?\n\nSome tasks are repetitive, while others need creativity and judgment. Smart AI use means choosing which tasks to give to AI so you keep building the skills that matter most.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/21ae4164d2398ffc77f5edf42d16e929-two_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-c16be7f1-46e7-4448-997e-d22428db25ea",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "Deeper Learning",
            "x": 6,
            "y": 8,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-44fd41c5-4038-4316-97e8-69e5e375959d",
            "width": 10
          },
          {
            "text": "Skills of the Future",
            "x": 43,
            "y": 26,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-e365cc66-bf8a-4df1-ae4d-4da6b0c457d9",
            "width": 10
          },
          {
            "text": "The Spell Checker Model",
            "x": 16,
            "y": 44,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-71536ebe-b760-4a4f-8904-5463b564b75d",
            "width": 11
          },
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 87,
            "y": 86,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-61c12f93-e668-4a3b-ab10-8b09009a01a3",
            "width": 15
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Deeper learning happens when students explain ideas, look at evidence, and solve problems on their own.\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/4d4bb0e110adb6b770e487ca4b1640b7-twoone_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-71536ebe-b760-4a4f-8904-5463b564b75d",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-c16be7f1-46e7-4448-997e-d22428db25ea",
            "width": 15
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "How do pilots keep their skills when autopilot does the flying?\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/61a4ca74aa0cd411acad917986dbf6b7-twotwo_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-e365cc66-bf8a-4df1-ae4d-4da6b0c457d9",
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 86,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-c16be7f1-46e7-4448-997e-d22428db25ea",
            "width": 15
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Spell checkers have improved writing accuracy for decades without replacing human authors.\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/7ae3658090bce2c5beb0170fb4a02304-twothree_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-44fd41c5-4038-4316-97e8-69e5e375959d",
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-c16be7f1-46e7-4448-997e-d22428db25ea",
            "width": 15
          }
        ],
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "How do pilots keep their skills when autopilot does the flying?\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/ef1a6a169593c94a5d1ed116cfa72ebd-three_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-0c70d15f-04dc-42e5-8c8e-6a62cafa5f48",
        "layout": "text-top-right",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "Practice Makes Permanent",
            "x": 13,
            "y": 15,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-7a996cfe-0d33-4b6d-acb8-d63d8e6b114e",
            "width": 18
          },
          {
            "text": "Better Together",
            "x": 42,
            "y": 16,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-bd952ac1-d8b8-41ef-b664-354663330928",
            "width": 17
          },
          {
            "text": "Staying in Command",
            "x": 19,
            "y": 72,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-9eff3e43-15b6-4bed-a52d-0a1b46844bee",
            "width": 21
          },
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 90,
            "y": 89,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-61c12f93-e668-4a3b-ab10-8b09009a01a3",
            "width": 16
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Like any skill, flying ability gets weaker without practice — so pilots train in simulators to stay prepared.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5fdcb0ceada286a4504caffb428d5ac9-threeone_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-7a996cfe-0d33-4b6d-acb8-d63d8e6b114e",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 85,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-0c70d15f-04dc-42e5-8c8e-6a62cafa5f48",
            "width": 16
          }
        ],
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Autopilot systems help pilots fly more safely than they could on their own.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/bfa8de2b3427f946e28db1b590b4f6c6-thretwo_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-bd952ac1-d8b8-41ef-b664-354663330928",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 84,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-0c70d15f-04dc-42e5-8c8e-6a62cafa5f48",
            "width": 14
          }
        ],
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "showContinueButton": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Using AI responsibly means staying focused, checking its work, and stepping in when something seems wrong.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/b4a9528caa68571c8dd40787c90f9d54-threthree_panel.png",
        "key": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-9eff3e43-15b6-4bed-a52d-0a1b46844bee",
        "links": [
          {
            "text": "< Back",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 84,
            "targetKey": "thinking_critically_lesson5_level2panels_2026-0c70d15f-04dc-42e5-8c8e-6a62cafa5f48",
            "width": 15
          }
        ],
        "layout": "text-top-left",
        "showContinueButton": true
      }
    ],
    "use_links": "true",
    "display_name": "Impact on Human Skills",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Explore how AI affects human skills",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/1300318f06910b4211a34df062ce0e5c-two.jpg"
  },
